From f5679a48eeb66247a9354a79882c573574646c5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 18:37:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 091/115] iio: qcom_smgr: don't hold the sensor lock across the
 report wait

Every raw sysfs read returns -ETIMEDOUT, on every sensor, with nothing
logged and a healthy QMI link underneath: the inventory enumerates all
sixteen sensors and the buffering subscription is accepted by the SLPI.

qcom_smgr_read_one() takes sensor->lock, asks for the subscription and
then waits on the report completion while still holding it. Publishing
last_values from qcom_smgr_buffering_report_handler() was moved under
that same lock to close a torn-read race, which put the complete() call
behind a mutex the waiter itself owns. The handler blocks, the
completion is never signalled, and the wait always runs its full HZ.

Drop the lock for the duration of the wait. The reference taken by
qcom_smgr_buffering_get() keeps the subscription alive while it is
released, and both last_values and the refcount are still only touched
with the lock held.

The buffered path does not wait on the completion, so by inspection it
is unaffected; that has not been measured.

Fixes: bde809e2905c ("iio: qcom_smgr: fix last_values data race and samp_freq slot routing")
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c b/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
index 0a5598d84988..2a30a6147b00 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
@@ -933,8 +933,17 @@ static int qcom_smgr_read_one(struct iio_dev *iio_dev,
 	if (ret)
 		goto out;
 
+	/*
+	 * Drop the lock across the wait. qcom_smgr_buffering_report_handler()
+	 * takes the same lock to publish last_values, so a waiter that holds it
+	 * makes the completion it is waiting for unreachable and every read
+	 * times out after exactly HZ with nothing logged. The reference taken
+	 * above keeps the subscription alive while the lock is dropped.
+	 */
+	mutex_unlock(&sensor->lock);
 	if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&sensor->report[data_type], HZ))
 		ret = -ETIMEDOUT;
+	mutex_lock(&sensor->lock);
 
 	qcom_smgr_buffering_put(smgr, sensor);
 
